<title>MEXICO: Mexico increasing corn output yields - Ag Min.</title>
<headline>Mexico increasing corn output yields - Ag Min.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican Agriculture Minister Francisco Labastida Ochoa said programs to boost corn yields are working across the country.</p>
<p>In a statement obtained Tuesday, the ministry said Labastida told a farmers' meeting that yields had risen in key states, as a result of the &quot;Kilo for Kilo&quot; scheme that aims to use improved seed types and optimise fertilizer use.</p>
<p>Labastida said yields in the states of Tlaxcala and Puebla had been raised to 4-5 tonnes per hectare from traditional yields of 1.5 tonnes. In Hidalgo state, yields in the last two years have gone up to 10-11 tonnes from 4 tonnes.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530.</p>
<p>E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
